#!/bin/sh
#
# Configured as part of the DigitalOcean 1-Click Image build process

cat <<EOF
********************************************************************************

Welcome to DigitalOcean's One-Click Herdr Droplet.

Herdr is the terminal runtime your coding agents run in. SSH in, run herdr,
and the agents below are already on PATH. You do not need to install them.

PREINSTALLED AGENTS:
  claude        Claude Code
  codex         OpenAI Codex CLI
  opencode      OpenCode
  grok          Grok Build
  kilo          Kilo Code CLI
  cursor-agent  Cursor Agent CLI

GETTING STARTED:

  1. Open Herdr (the server is already running):
       herdr

  2. In a pane, start an agent from /root/workspace or any project:
       claude
       codex
       opencode
       grok
       kilo
       cursor-agent

  3. Detach with Ctrl-b then q. Agents keep running. Reattach with herdr.

CONNECT FROM YOUR LAPTOP:

  Install Herdr on the laptop (https://herdr.dev/docs/install/), then add
  ~/.ssh/config. The Host name is what you pass to herdr --remote:

    Host herdr-droplet
      HostName your-droplet-ip
      User root
      IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519

  Check the alias from the laptop, exit that shell, then attach:
    ssh herdr-droplet
    exit
    herdr --remote herdr-droplet

  Or skip the config entry:
    herdr --remote ssh://root@your-droplet-ip

  Detach with Ctrl-b then q. Agents keep running on this Droplet.

Each agent still needs its own login the first time you start it. Herdr
integrations for these agents are already installed, so Herdr can restore
their sessions after a server restart.

Sign-in helpers:
  Claude Code:   claude
  Codex:         codex login
  OpenCode:      opencode auth login
  Grok Build:    grok login --device-auth
  Kilo Code:     kilo auth
  Cursor:        cursor-agent login

Helper commands:
  Status:          /opt/status-herdr.sh
  Start server:    /opt/start-herdr.sh
  Stop server:     /opt/stop-herdr.sh
  Restart server:  /opt/restart-herdr.sh
  Update Herdr:    /opt/update-herdr.sh
  Update agents:   /opt/update-agents.sh

Documentation: https://herdr.dev/docs/

********************************************************************************
To delete this message of the day: rm -rf $(readlink -f ${0})
EOF
